​4. Statement Tag Generation (T300-FETCH-GECT-AMT & DO-PERFORM-TILL)
​For every eligible transaction found:
​Edit Mask Checks: Calls utility UT0022 using the transaction code (WA-TRAN-CODE). If bit 7 of the input table is set (WA-INPUT-PARAM-TABLE(7) = 1), the transaction is suppressed.  
​Balance Calculation: Computes the opening balance as WA-BAL - WA-AMT1.  
​Header Tags Emission (DO-PERFORM-FIELDS):
​Selects TXN_CMP_SSR.NEXTVAL from DUAL.  
​Formats and writes SWIFT Basic Header Block 1 and Application Header Block 2 ({1:F01...}{2:I940...}{4:) via A300-GENERATE-BIC.  
​Generates Tag :20: (Transaction Reference Number).  
​Generates Tag :25: (Account identification with check-digit computed via utility UT0151).  
​Generates Tag :28C: (Statement/sequence number, e.g., :28C:NNNNN/00001).  
​Generates Tag :60F: (Opening balance with Credit/Debit marker 'C' or 'D', transaction date YYMMDD, currency code, and formatted amount with comma decimal notation).  
​Statement Line & Narration Tags Emission:
​Queries GECT (TRAN_TYPE = '85') and FXTX to retrieve deal date, branch reference (WA-BR-REF), and correspondence reference (WA-CORR-REF).  
​If transaction code is 20045 or 20055, executes P100-REFNO-NTRF to fetch narrative reference from GECT (TRAN_TYPE = '20') and replaces WA-PART-BR-REF.  
​Generates Tag :61: (Value date, entry date, Debit/Credit indicator, transaction amount, transaction type NTRF, branch reference, and correspondence reference).  
​Writes the MFX serial number on a subsequent record line.  
​Generates Tag :86: (Calls UT0250 using WA-TRAN-CODE to obtain the transaction description and outputs :86:<TRAN_CODE>:<DESC>).  
​5. Statement Tail & Closing Balance (A101-GENERATE-TAIL / A405-GENERATE-62)
​Once all transactions for the account are read (or if no transactions exist, where it queries table GLDM for CUM_CURR_VAL as fallback opening/closing balance):  
​Computes the final balance: WA-CLOS-AMNT = WA-OPEN-BAL-TEM + WA-TEMP-AMNT.  
​Generates Tag :62F: (Final Closing Balance with 'C'/'D' sign, date, currency, and decimal amount).  
​Writes the SWIFT message trailer delimiter "-}$" to conclude the MT940 block.  
​6. Blocked Accounts Processing & Program Shutdown
​Blocked BGL Accounts (A75082 / B100-READ-BLOCK-BGLS): Once cursor CUR1 finishes (SQLCODE = 1403), it reads blocked accounts defined in card file $card/SSRBGLBLOCK.card into an internal array and runs G100-GECT-DETAILS for each blocked account.  
​Cleanup (A600-CLOSE & A800-STOP): Closes all SQL cursors (GETDETL1, GETDETL3, GETDETL4, CUR1), closes PRNTFILE, calls DBIO function 91 to disconnect from the database, and terminates execution (STOP RUN).  
